Code
- Parts of core/ (blosc/chunk decoding, grids, rasteriser) and the overlay drawing and LightningCast parsing are derived from wxqt-grib
  (https://github.com/intelati26/wxqt-grib), GPLv3.
- core/third_party/zstd: Zstandard single-file decompressor, Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates, used under its BSD license
  (core/third_party/zstd/LICENSE.txt; also available under GPLv2).
- gradlew, gradlew.bat and gradle/wrapper: Gradle, Apache License 2.0.

Sounding calculations
- The parcel, shear, helicity, storm motion, composite-parameter and hazard-type calculations of the sounding screen follow SHARPpy (BSD 3-clause) by way of
  wxqt-grib's Kotlin-ported engine (SharpProfile, SharpParcel, SharpIndices, SharpAnalysis, SharpPrecip, SharpSars with its SPC analogue databases, SharpTornadoProb); the attribution and license text are in docs/sharppy-notice.md.
- Model profiles: Iowa State University's BUFKIT feed (https://meteor.geol.iastate.edu/data/bufkit/) of NCEP's RRFS and GFS output (public domain model data).

Map lines (androidApp/src/main/assets/statev2.f32, county.f32, ca.f32, mx.f32)
- Taken from the wX project (GPLv3, https://gitlab.com/joshua.tee/wx). wX's own source for the underlying boundaries has not been
  traced; if you know it, please record it here.

Data (fetched at run time, not redistributed except small test fixtures)
- NOAA / NWS: SPC REFS and outlooks, MRMS, National Blend of Models (public domain).
- LightningCast: CIMSS / University of Wisconsin-Madison (https://cimss.ssec.wisc.edu); check their terms before redistributing.
